# Project Overview

This is a REST API for managing To-Do tasks.

## Technology Stack

- Node.js
- Express.js 5
- JavaScript ES Modules
- Zod for validation
- Node.js built-in test runner

## Coding Rules

- Use JavaScript only. Never use TypeScript.
- Use ES module imports and exports.
- Keep route handlers separate from business logic.
- Keep business logic inside the services directory.
- Use async/await where appropriate.
- Use meaningful variable and function names.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.

## API Standards

- Follow REST API conventions.
- Validate incoming request data using Zod.
- Return consistent JSON responses.
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Handle errors through centralized middleware.

## Testing

- Write tests for API endpoints.
- Cover success and failure scenarios.
- Run npm test after making changes.

## General Instructions

- Inspect the existing project before modifying files.
- Follow the existing folder structure.
- Do not introduce unnecessary architectural complexity.
- Explain important changes after implementation.
